  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTION ECOLOGICAL ENHANCEMENT &amp; M</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Santiaguillo Lagoon, located in the state of Durango, Mxico, is considered one of the 30 most important wetlands in North America because it harbors a large amount of migratory birds. It covers 83% of the total surface of identified wetlands in the state of Durango, and it is a key site in Mxico for the wintering of Mexican duck, Northern pintail, white-fronted goose and snow goose. Through this project, key partners and stakeholders will implement the strategies established in the Santiaguillo Lagoon Environment Agenda by establishing the Ejido Conservation Reserve to conserve 2,471 acres through a private land conservation contract; building a filtering pit to reduce siltation into the Santiaguillo Lagoon; constructing water control structures in the Ejido Conservation Reserve to promote infiltration and reduce erosion; and developing a cattle management plan within the Ejido Conservation Reserve to restore ecosystems and improve cattle raising techniques.</narrative>
  </description>
